<Item XName="Note" UserName="Note" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;FONT size=2 face=TimesNewRoman&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoBodyText align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: Arial; FONT-SIZE: 18pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoBodyText align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: Arial; FONT-SIZE: 18pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Digital Modulation&amp;nbsp;Tx and Rx (with Fast Decision Feedback&amp;nbsp;Equalizer)&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: Arial; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;U&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Example Workspace&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=center&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;This workspace is to demostrate Digital Modulation&amp;nbsp;source and receiver using SystemVue data flow model and MATLAB Script model. &lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;The source consists of Preamble and data Payload parts. Both Preamble and data Payload part can be set as BPSK, QPSK, 8-PSK, 16-QAM, 32-QAM, 64-QAM, 128-QAM, 256-QAM, 512-QAM, 1024-QAM, 2048-QAM, 4096-QAM, 16-APSK, 32-APSK, 16 Star-QAM, 32 Star-QAM and Custom APSK. Transmit shaping filter can be selected as Raised Cosine or Root Raised Cosine. The bandwidth is determined by the ChipRate parameter. Oversampling ratio is determined by SampsPerChip parameter.&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;In the receiver side, it consists of receiver filter (Root Raised Cosine or No), frame synchronization, automatic gain control (AGC), carrier&amp;nbsp;frequency synchronization, carrier phase estimator. The equalizer&amp;nbsp;is the fast computation MMSE Decision feedback&amp;nbsp;Equalizer. &lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P align=left&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;</Text>
<Item XName="Page" Type="PageMgr">
<Item XName="Display0" Type="NotesDisp">
<DVport><T>Array_Dbl64</T><D>1;4;;;Gc14;am14</D></DVport>
<PVPort><T>Array_Dbl64</T><D>1;4;;;Vg}f{dgYT24;jms2SBO}b24</D></PVPort>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>1</D></Show>
<ShowCmd><T>Int</T><D>1</D></ShowCmd>
<Window><T>Array_I64</T><D>1;4;I9;;OC;q4</D></Window>
<ZOrder><T>Int</T><D>7</D></ZOrder></Item></Item></Item>
<Item XName="Page" Type="PageMgr" />
<Item XName="Theoretical_512-QAM_BER" UserName="Theoretical_512-QAM_BER" Type="Equation">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>EbNodB_512=0:1:26&#x000D;&#x000A;EbNo=10.^(EbNodB_512/10);&#x000D;&#x000A;%512-QAM BER&#x000D;&#x000A;k=9;&#x000D;&#x000A;M=2^k;&#x000D;&#x000A;x=sqrt(3*k*EbNo/(M-1));&#x000D;&#x000A;QAM_512_Pb=(4/k)*(1-1/sqrt(M))*(1/2)*erfc(x/sqrt(2));&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;</Text>
<UnitUse><T>Int</T><D>2</D></UnitUse>
